/* book Worked example 2: Q: A silicon IMPATT diode (vs = 10⁵ m/s) is to work at 10 GHz. (a) Find the drift length. (b) What drift length is needed at 94 GHz? (c) If it is biased at 100 V and 50 mA and delivers 0.5 W, find its efficiency.
   1. f ≈ vs/(2Ld), so Ld = vs/(2f) = 10⁵/(2 × 10¹⁰) = 5 × 10⁻⁶ m = 5 µm.
   2. At 94 GHz: Ld = 10⁵/(2 × 94 × 10⁹) = 0.53 µm, so millimetre-wave IMPATTs are very thin.
   3. DC input = 100 × 0.050 = 5 W; η = 0.5/5 = 10 %.
   4. Check: the transit time Ld/vs = 50 ps is half the 100 ps period, as the formula intends.
   Answer: Ld = 5 µm at 10 GHz and 0.53 µm at 94 GHz; efficiency 10 %. */
