/* book Worked example: Q: A WR-90 slotted line (a = 22.86 mm) is used with a voltage-calibrated VSWR meter. With an unknown load: Vmax = 3.0, Vmin = 1.2, adjacent minima are 19.9 mm apart, and the first minimum is 6.0 mm from the load. Find the VSWR, |Γ|, the return loss, λg, the frequency and the normalised load impedance.
   1. S = 3.0/1.2 = 2.5; |Γ| = (2.5 − 1)/(2.5 + 1) = 1.5/3.5 = 0.429; return loss = −20 log₁₀ 0.429 = 7.36 dB.
   2. λg = 2 × 19.9 = 39.8 mm. (The old trap: λg is never 19.9 mm.)
   3. λc = 2a = 45.72 mm. 1/λ₀² = 1/39.8² + 1/45.72² = 6.313 × 10⁻⁴ + 4.784 × 10⁻⁴ = 1.1097 × 10⁻³ mm⁻², so λ₀ = 30.02 mm and f = c/λ₀ = 9.99 GHz. Note λg > λ₀, as in any hollow guide.
   4. βdmin = 360° × 6.0/39.8 = 54.27°; tan 54.27° = 1.392.
   5. zL = (1 − j2.5 × 1.392)/(2.5 − j1.392) = (1 − j3.480)/(2.5 − j1.392) = 0.896 − j0.892.
   6. Check: ΓL = (zL − 1)/(zL + 1) = 0.429∠−71.5°, and |ΓL| matches 0.429.
   Answer: S = 2.5, |Γ| = 0.429, RL = 7.36 dB, λg = 39.8 mm, f = 9.99 GHz, zL = 0.896 − j0.892 (a capacitive load). */
