/* book exam traps: Taking the distance between adjacent minima as λg. It is λg/2. | Square-rooting readings from a voltage-calibrated VSWR meter, or not square-rooting power readings. Check how the meter is calibrated first. | Finding λg smaller than λ₀ in a waveguide. In a hollow guide λg > λ₀ always; a smaller value means a reading error. | Measuring a high VSWR from Vmax/Vmin directly. Above about 10 use the double-minimum method, S ≈ λg/(πW). | Trusting uncalibrated VNA data. Without SOLT (or TRL) correction, directivity and port match errors can make a good part look bad or a bad part look good. */
