/* book Worked example 2: Q: An on-chip spiral of 2 nH has Q = 12 at 2 GHz. (a) Find its series resistance. (b) Placed in series in a 50 Ω line, what is |S₂₁| and the power lost in it? (c) A 0.5 mm bond wire (about 0.5 nH) joins a hybrid amplifier at 10 GHz: find its reactance.
   1. X = ωL = 2π × 2 × 10⁹ × 2 × 10⁻⁹ = 25.13 Ω; R = X/Q = 25.13/12 = 2.09 Ω.
   2. Series impedance Z = 2.09 + j25.13 Ω between 50 Ω ports: S₂₁ = 2Z₀/(2Z₀ + Z) = 100/(102.09 + j25.13); |S₂₁| = 100/105.1 = 0.951, that is 0.44 dB.
   3. Power absorbed in R as a fraction of the available power: |I|²R/Pavailable = 4Z₀R/|2Z₀ + Z|² = 200 × 2.09/105.1² = 0.038, so 3.8 % heats the spiral; the rest of the 0.44 dB is reflected by the mismatch.
   4. Bond wire: X = 2π × 10 × 10⁹ × 0.5 × 10⁻⁹ = 31.4 Ω, more than half of 50 Ω, so it must be part of the matching design.
   Answer: R = 2.09 Ω; |S₂₁| = 0.951 (0.44 dB), with 3.8 % of the power absorbed in the spiral; the bond wire is +j31.4 Ω at 10 GHz. */
